'''Scout troopers''', also known as '''biker scouts''', were a specialized [[stormtrooper]] variant used by the [[Galactic Empire]] on a range of missions, which mostly involved [[Scout|reconnaissance]]. In particular, scout troopers often used the [[74-Z speeder bike]]. They had [[Scout trooper armor|lighter armor]] than standard [[trooper]]s, much like their urban counterparts, [[patrol trooper]]s, who used [[C-PH patrol speeder bike]]s to navigate dense urban environments.

==Overview==
Succeeding the [[clone scout trooper]]s of the [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="Geektionary" /> scout troopers served as a reconnaissance force for the [[Galactic Empire]]. They were trained for more independence and adaptability than other Imperial troops.<ref name="Scout Trooper DB">{{Databank|scout-troopers|Scout Troopers}}</ref> While described as an elite special forces branch that existed outside the rank-and-file [[Stormtrooper Corps]],<ref name="Emperor's Finest">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2018/9/17/the-emperors-finest|text=The Emperor's Finest}}</ref> many scout troopers were often assigned regular deployment alongside standard [[stormtrooper]] forces,<ref name="Fallen Order" /><ref name="Jedi: Survivor" /> with one scout trooper, [[Rick]], even working as a door technician in addition to a [[trooper]] capacity.<ref name="Jedi: Survivor" /> Indeed, there existed scout troopers described as "elite" scout troopers, signifying their status as above standard members of their organization: the [[Ghost Lancers]], for example, were an entire [[company]] of elite scout troopers who searched for [[Imperial Academy]] graduates that met their standards.<ref name="Winner's Circle">{{StoryCite|story=Gone to the Winner's Circle|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref> All the same, scout troopers in general were seen as more elite [[soldier]]s than the standard stormtrooper.<ref name="Products legion expansion">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/products/star-wars-legion/products/scout-troopers-unit-expansion|text=Scout Troopers Unit Expansion}}</ref>

Scout troopers were often stationed at Imperial bases, [[City|cities]], [[planet]]s, and other points of interest. A famous example was the [[Death Star's shield generator]] on [[Endor]],<ref name="Scout Trooper DB" /> where elite scout troopers were stationed.<ref name="218 Launchpad">{{InsiderCite|218|Launchpad}}</ref> Utilizing [[speeder bike]]s, scout troopers patrolled [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] areas, maintaining law and order and looking out for possible attackers.<ref name="Scout Trooper DB" /> This is how they get their nickname of "biker scouts." Scout troopers may also be seen patrolling areas on foot, as seen on planets like [[Endor]]<ref name="Episode VI" /> and [[Vardos]].<ref name="BF2" />

[[File:DLT-19xSniper-SWL.png|thumb|left|250px|A scout trooper sniper targets enemy forces with a DLT-19x targeting blaster.]]
Scout troopers fulfilled their reconnaissance role in other ways as well. They were often sent to [[scout]] out enemies during a battle to gain information to report back to their [[Officer|commander]]. Similarly, they may be sent on a reconnaissance mission to gain information on an individual or group when there isn't a current battle going on. Scout troopers also may be tasked with an [[Spy|espionage]] mission, getting behind enemy lines and gaining secret information. All three of these types of reconnaissance missions may be long term.<ref name="Scout Trooper DB" /> Also within their ranks were the [[Stormtrooper sniper|sniper troopers]], who utilized long range rifles for a wide variety of missions.<ref name="BF2" /> Sniper troopers may provide long range cover for [[stormtrooper]]s during a mission. Sniper troopers may also be sent on similar reconnaissance missions, so if necessary, they can take out key targets from a distance.<ref name="Commander" />

Scout troopers were regarded as the finest marksmen in the [[Stormtrooper Corps]], thus making them the best fit for sniper troopers and were often used as [[assassin]]s.<ref name="Commander" /> Scout troopers were also trained in the opposite. When blasters were deemed insufficient, scout troopers were equipped with [[Electro riot baton|electrobaton]]s for melee combat. When [[Jedi]] were spotted, scout troopers were often sent to use their electrobatons against the Jedi's [[lightsaber]]. Scout troopers were stationed on several different planets with electro-batons. They patrolled these planets and fought against any Jedi they spotted. They also often had trouble with the local [[Species|fauna]] on planets such as [[Zeffo]] and [[Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Fallen Order" /> A further variant of scout trooper, known as [[Shield Trooper]]s, used an electro-baton in combination with a physical shield.<ref name="Jedi: Survivor" /> Scout troopers were also skilled in infiltration,<ref name="Scout Trooper DB" /> usually using [[EE-4 carbine rifle]]s to sneak into enemy controlled positions and capture them for the Empire.<ref name="BF2" />

==History==
[[File:LittleAphra-2016DoctorAphra34.jpg|thumb|right|270px|Scout troopers find [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] on [[Arbiflux]].]]
During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], many scout troopers were deployed throughout Imperial territory. Scout troopers equipped with [[Electro riot baton|electrobaton]]s were stationed at [[Zeffo]], at the [[Imperial Refinery]] on [[Kashyyyk]], and in the [[Fortress Inquisitorius]] on Nur. Many scout troopers, while patrolling with electrobatons, encountered and were killed by [[Padawan]] turned [[Jedi Knight]] [[Cal Kestis]] during the [[secret mission to rebuild the Jedi Order]]<ref name="Fallen Order" /> and subsequent [[Stinger Mantis crew's crusade against the Empire|crusade against the Empire]]. One scout trooper named Rick served as a door technician in [[Imperial Post 8L-055]], where Rick encountered Kestis.<ref name="Jedi: Survivor" /> Scout troopers served against the [[Free Ryloth Movement]] during the [[Ryloth Insurgency]].<ref name="HH">{{Rebels|Hera's Heroes}}</ref> On [[Lothal]], scout troopers were part of the protection for the [[excavation of the Lothal Jedi Temple]]. Padawan [[Ezra Bridger]] and [[Mandalorian]] [[Sabine Wren]] of the [[Spectres]] stole armor from [[LS-412]] and [[LS-515]] to [[Mission to the Lothal Jedi Temple|infiltrate]] the Temple.<ref name="Wolves and a Door">{{Rebels|Wolves and a Door}}</ref>

Scout troopers could be found aboard [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader's]] personal [[fleet]], [[Death Squadron]]. One of the scout troopers' priorities were to aid the [[Sith Lord]] in crushing the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] along with its sympathizers and secret allies.<ref name="Ultimate SW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> Several scout troopers were part of [[Captain]] [[Magna Tolvan]]'s force stationed on the [[moon]] of [[Yavin 4]] after the Rebellion [[Evacuation of Yavin 4|abandoned]] the [[Great Temple]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra 3">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 3|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 3]]</ref>

[[File:Scout_Trooper_Biker_SWB.png|thumb|left|250px|A scout trooper riding a 74-Z speeder bike on Endor.]]
Elite scout troopers,<ref name="218 Launchpad" /> such as the [[Ghost Lancers]] company,<ref name="Winner's Circle" /> protected the [[Death Star's shield generator]] on [[Endor]]<ref name="Episode VI" /> in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> which shielded the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]] over the [[forest]] [[moon]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> While the Empire had first used [[All Terrain Armored Transport]]s and [[All Terrain Scout Transport]]s for the reconnaissance of areas that had been cleared, the underbrush and woodland terrain of the moon was inappropriate for the majority of Imperial vehicles due to their large size and stature. Therefore, most of the vehicular patrol duty was conducted by scout troopers on fast [[74-Z speeder bike]]s. Despite the threat that Endor's tall trees posed, the forest's many trails could be used for safe travel.<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> At least six scout troopers encountered [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Han Solo]], [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], and [[Chewbacca]] whilst on patrol. Scout troopers later participated in the [[Battle of Endor]].<ref name="Episode VI" />

Scout troopers also participated in the [[Battle of Jakku]].<ref name="BF2">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|8}}</ref> [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] operated an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]], which included scout troopers.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

==Equipment==
===Overview===
[[File:Biker_Scout_DICE.png|thumb|right|230px|A scout trooper with a DLT-19 heavy blaster rifle.]]
Scout troopers commonly utilized [[614-AvA speeder bike]]s<ref name="HH" /> and 74-Z [[speeder bike]]s,<ref name="Episode VI" /> as well as [[All Terrain Reconnaissance Transport]]s.<ref name="Vader 8">[[Darth Vader (2015) 8|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 8]]</ref>

Scout trooper helmets could be retracted up while still being worn, allowing the wearer's face to be revealed unlike regular [[stormtrooper]] helmets.<ref name="HH" /> Under their [[armor]] they wore a [[body glove]]. Their [[cummerbund]] had two pouches which was commonly used for storing [[Ration pack|survival rations]]. On the back of their breastplate they had a power unit [[backpack]] which could also store extra gear. In their boot was a holster for their [[EC-17 hold-out blaster|blaster pistol]].<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

